  "id": "COMPOUND:31358 - PROTEIN:5867",
  "verbalization": "Brusatol is implicated in the biological pathway leading to HaCaT cells through multiple indirect mechanisms. The evidence suggests that Brusatol acts as a target for several molecular entities, including MOVP-3 and Carboxylesterase 2, which in turn target 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. This compound is ultimately shown to have a target of HaCaT cells. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Brusatol in modulating cellular processes through the activation of downstream targets, possibly involving enzyme inhibition or signaling pathways. The evidence supports a mechanism where Brusatol indirectly influences HaCaT cells via a series of molecular interactions, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
